\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{An actual retained four-point response}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{In the three-coordinate model of \ref{fdip-0047}, retain the
coordinate #{x} and choose #{f=(1,0,0)}. Its covariance and quartic
couplings give #{Q^{-1}f=(1,1,1)} and #{g_v=1} at all three
coordinates. Substituting in \ref{fdip-00GP} yields
##{\left.\frac{\extd}{\extd\lambda}\kappa_{4,\lambda}(x)\right|_{0+}
 =-(1^4+1^4+1^4)=-3,}
and hence #{\kappa_{4,\lambda}(x)=-3\lambda+O(\lambda^2)} as
#{\lambda\downarrow0}. The full-law calculation and the exact
retained law agree by \ref{fdip-00GO}.}

\p{The coefficient is the same as in the formal calculation, now
with an actual right-hand remainder and a non-Gaussian retained law
for sufficiently small positive coupling. The higher coefficients
and generated sextic term already computed in \ref{fdip-0047}
use the same moments; \ref{fdip-00GN} supplies their finite-order
compact-set interpretation for the fiber interaction.}
